# V. Risk factors

#1. AI pricing pressure
AI Agent may subvert the traditional SaaS per-seat pricing model. If AI can automatically handle a large volume of work streams that previously required manual work, the enterprise may reduce the number of seats purchased by Servicenow, thereby compressing single-client income.

#2. Super-large cloud producers compete
The big platforms like Power Platform, Salesforce, and AWS are all investing in the business workflow. These companies have greater customer penetration and tied marketing capacity, which may encroach on the share of ServiceNow’s market.

#3 Acquisition of integration risks
The recent acquisition of companies such as Moveworks (AI Dialogue), Armis (Security), Veza (Data Governance) will increase the cost of integration and reduce profit margins in the short term. If integration is not successful, it may slow growth.

##4. Natural patterns of growth deceleration
The 20% plus increase is increasingly difficult to maintain on the $13 billion income base. Once the acceleration slides below 15%, the valuation multipliers may face further compression.

##5. Client budget cuts
Macroeconomic uncertainties can lead to tighter IT budgets for enterprises, especially where workflow automation projects are often less "indispensible" than core ERP projects.

