# Six, investment arguments

# Look at logic (3 bars)

1. ** Workstream platform is not an alternative:** Servicenow has become a "workstream operating system" for large enterprises, embedded deep across IT, HR, customer service, security etc. 97% subscription income, 80% plus Māori, 26% RPO acceleration, all of which attests to the high stickyness and increasing intensity of clients
**AI is a catalyst rather than a threat:** Servicenow is embedding the AI functionality into the platform to help the enterprise to automate it at a higher level. AI is not replacing Servicenow, but making the Servicenow platform more valuable - the enterprise needs a unified platform to deploy and manage AI Agency
3. ** Historical low valuation:** approximately 22 times PE in the forward, approximately 20 times EV/FCF, and 0.88 in the lowest range since the company was listed. For one leader, SaaS, which maintains a 20% + increase, 30% free cash flow profit margin, this valuation level is extremely rare.

# Look at empty logic (3 bars)

1. **AI Uncertainty in the shift of pricing patterns:** If AI Agent makes seat-based pricing obsolete, Servicenow needs to redesign the business model. The income growth and profitability of the transition period may be subject to pressure at the same time
2. **Execution risk during merger and digestion:** Multiple large acquisitions in the short term have increased the complexity of integration. If the Moveworks/Armis/Veza do not produce synergies quickly, the profit margin will be held back, and market tolerance of the profit margin is low in the current environment
3. **The valuation may still have downside space:** Although PE has been significantly compressed, the market may give a lower number of valuations in the context of AI Subversive Enterprise Software narrative. Historically, SaaS has been able to reduce its valuations to 15-18 times the forward PE at the speed of the surge.

