# VII. Conclusion

** The study is worth studying, but independent judgement on AI price shocks is needed**

Servicenow is the absolute leader in the area of corporate workflow automation, and is still able to maintain 20% + acceleration, 80% + Māori, ~30% free cash flow profitability on a $10 billion scale. Stock prices are only 22 times higher, PEG < 1, and are historically low in valuation terms.

The core uncertainty is the impact of AI on the pricing model of enterprise software. If AI ultimately proves to be making a big cake (more AI Agent per Agent on the Servicenow platform, paying fees), it is currently an excellent point of entry; if AI proves to be a reduced cake (reduced demand for workflow platforms by human users), there is still room for down-scaling the valuation.

It is recommended that the focus be on: the AI pricing model of Servicenow (on the basis of Agent or consumption), the actual customers of Now Assist using data, and trends in renewal and expansion of large clients.

